"""E4 extension (PREREG_AMENDMENTS A11): instrumented SUL/GUL (WWW'26) runs on UB-GOLD folds.

Same CLI and per-run JSON "part" schema as evalpaper/harness/run_eval.py:
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B run_method.py --method SUL-GUL --dataset BZR --fold 0 [--hp hpfree]

* The official repository (ZhenyuYangMQ/UncertaintyGLAD @ 1a1f2e4, src/, byte-identical, no license) implements
  only the GUL framework ("demo code for the GUL framework", src/README.md); SUL is not released. The method is
  labelled "SUL-GUL" in run ids (naming convention) and meta.variant = "GUL".
* GUL's training and scoring code is used verbatim: U_GLAD (src/model.py), GIN (src/layers.py), load_args /
  compute_metrics (src/utils.py). The training loop below is a line-by-line copy of src/main.py:run_split();
  every change is marked "# CHANGE" and listed in NOTES.md (D1-D8).
* Normal-only mode (A11): GUL's poll_ratio only acts in its data loader (src/data_loader.py:25-30), which is
  replaced by the UB-GOLD folds (training = normal graphs only). meta.hparams.poll_ratio is set to 0 to record it.
* Folds, features, seeds and the held-out normals come from the harness itself (its run_eval.py is imported,
  never modified): UB-GOLD get_ad_split_TU / get_ad_dataset_TU, asserted against
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ubgold_splits, set_seed(3407+fold), RandomState(2026+1000*fold) carve-out.
* hp 'ubgold' = the released configuration = the README MUTAG demo line `python3 main.py` (no options; used for
  every dataset); hp 'hpfree' = repository argparse defaults. They resolve to the same options (NOTES.md).
* GUL evaluates the test graphs after every epoch, so every epoch is an evaluation point (eval_freq = 1).

Outputs (EP_PARTS / EP_SCORES / EP_CKPT override):
  evalpaper/ext/parts/<run_id>.json                         meta + per-epoch metrics
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ext_sulgul/scores/<run_id>.npz         per-graph test / held-out scores
  $GLAD_DATA_ROOT/ext_sulgul/ckpt/<DS>/<run_id>.pt       resumable state (removed when done)
"""
